  "653b79b3-daa1-43c5-bca5-cf99ae853fcc": {
   "id": "653b79b3-daa1-43c5-bca5-cf99ae853fcc",
   "message": {
    "id": "653b79b3-daa1-43c5-bca5-cf99ae853fcc",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1763436675.9,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "```python\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.metrics import cohen_kappa_score, confusion_matrix\n\na = pd.read_csv(\"minsun.csv\").rename(columns={\"label\": \"minsun\"})\nb = pd.read_csv(\"xiaohang.csv\").rename(columns={\"label\": \"xiaohang\"})\nm = a.merge(b, on=\"window_id\", how=\"inner\")\nprint(len(m), \"windows in both\")\n\nprint(\"kappa:\", round(cohen_kappa_score(m.minsun, m.xiaohang), 3))\nlabels = sorted(set(m.minsun) | set(m.xiaohang))\ncm = pd.DataFrame(confusion_matrix(m.minsun, m.xiaohang, labels=labels),\n                  index=[f\"M:{l}\" for l in labels], columns=[f\"X:{l}\" for l in labels])\nprint(cm)\n```\n\nIf `len(m)` isn't 200, someone skipped or duplicated a window. Check `a.window_id.duplicated().sum()` first."
     ]
    },
